# 🌴 Sun, Sand, and Services: Tourism and Household Welfare in Jamaica

![Tourism Map of Jamaica](/assets/images/jamaica_tourism_map.png){: width="100%" style="margin-bottom: 1em;" }

## 🎯 Motivation
Tourism is a cornerstone of Jamaica’s development strategy. But how much does it actually improve the lives of local households? This project investigates whether increased tourist spending translates into better welfare outcomes for Jamaican families — especially those outside the capital.

## 📊 Key Findings
- A $10M increase in tourist accommodation spending leads to a ~1% rise in real per-capita household expenditures in urban areas outside Kingston.
- Gains are strongest for medium-skilled workers in non-tourism services and manufacturing.
- Households in the middle of the expenditure distribution benefit most.
- Surprisingly, tourism workers themselves see limited gains — pointing to stagnant productivity in the sector.

